{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Two wives, one beloved and one hated</b> Multiplies wives, multiplies sorceries. This teaches: once he has two wives, the first practices sorcery so that he will hate the second." "<b>and the firstborn son shall be of the hated one</b> This is the son of the hated one, who is among the nine categories enumerated in Nedarim. Therefore Scripture juxtaposes to it the rebellious son — that the son will be rebellious." "<b>to the hated one</b> Letters: לנשאיה (to her father-in-law). To teach: hated in her marriages, which are disqualified. In the Midrash: \"for a man\" — this is the Holy One, blessed be He. \"Beloved\" — these are the idolaters, to whom He shows His face. \"Hated\" — these are Israel, from whom He hides His face."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The reference is to the phrase בני השנואה (son of the hated one) appearing among nine listings in tractate Nedarim; the exact list and its relation are uncertain but the translation follows the text literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:12.943114770Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}